 {r}←∆SetOpenProjects list;refs;ref
⍝ Defines what `U.GetOpenProjects` reports as the open projects, and therefore what
⍝ `EstablishProject` acts on. `list` must be a matrix with a namespace name in [;1] and a
⍝ folder in [;2]; a matrix with no rows at all means "no project is open".\\
⍝ Pass `⎕NULL` in order to remove the override again.\\
⍝ A user command executes its code either in `#.APLGit2.APLGit2` or in `⎕SE.APLGit2` - see
⍝ `GetRefToAPLGit2` - so both are catered for. Mind that when APLGit2 was loaded as a Tatin
⍝ package then `⎕SE.APLGit2` is that package's API namespace, so `U` is a sibling of it rather
⍝ than a child: that's what `##` is for.
 r←⍬
 refs←⍬
 :If 9=#.⎕NC'APLGit2.APLGit2.U'
     refs,←#.APLGit2.APLGit2.U
 :EndIf
 :If 9=⎕SE.⎕NC'APLGit2'
     :If 9=⎕SE.APLGit2.⎕NC'U'
         refs,←⎕SE.APLGit2.U
     :ElseIf 9=⎕SE.APLGit2.##.⎕NC'U'
         refs,←⎕SE.APLGit2.##.U
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
 'Found no namespace "U" the override could be established in'Assert 0<≢refs
 :For ref :In refs
     :If ⎕NULL≡list
         {}ref.⎕EX'∆OPEN_PROJECTS'
     :Else
         ref.∆OPEN_PROJECTS←list
     :EndIf
 :EndFor
⍝Done
